Rather than trusting a single feature,

the model integrates multiple imperfect observations to infer the most probable hidden state.

---

## 8. Execution Strategy

Institutional trading is designed to minimize information leakage.

Execution methods include

- VWAP
- TWAP
- Iceberg Orders
- Dark Pools

Execution strategy determines

how much observable evidence reaches the public market.

Therefore,

observable evidence depends not only on institutional intention,

but also on execution style.

---

## 9. Observable Evidence Depends On Execution

Institution Decision

↓

Execution Strategy

↓

Observable Market Features

Different execution strategies leave different market footprints.

Therefore,

identical institutional intentions may produce very different observable data.

---

## 10. Model Limitations

No statistical model can recover information that never appears in the data.

If institutions successfully hide their activity,

observable evidence becomes weak.

This represents an information limitation,

not necessarily a model limitation.

---

## 11. Institutional Footprints

The model does not directly identify institutions.

Instead,

it estimates whether observable market behaviour is statistically consistent with institutional activity.

Observable features therefore represent

institutional footprints,

not institutional actions themselves.

---

## 12. Hidden States

HMM discovers statistical regimes.

Researchers then interpret these regimes economically.

Example

State 1

↓

Positive OFI

Positive Main Flow

Positive VWAP

↓

Interpreted as

Accumulation

The interpretation is validated using external evidence such as 13F.

---

## 13. Why 13F Matters

13F does not validate the HMM algorithm.

Instead,

it validates whether the economic interpretation of the hidden state is reasonable.

If the estimated accumulation state corresponds to future increases in institutional holdings,

the hidden-state interpretation becomes more credible.

---

## 14. Validation vs Backtesting

13F Validation answers

> Did we estimate institutional positions correctly?

Backtesting answers

> Can estimated institutional positions generate profitable trading strategies?

These are fundamentally different questions.

Research should validate hidden states before evaluating trading performance.

